Blur, shadows, borders, and antialiased coverage of vector rectangles at
screen edges. Each screen-edges.ass image contains eight colored objects:
one at each of the four sides and four corners.

screen-edges.ass samples:
  1000: Gaussian blur from rectangles wholly outside the screen.
  3000: Gaussian blur on rectangles crossing the screen boundaries.
  5000: Gaussian blur on non-square rectangles with fractional placement.
  7000: Blurred shadows cast inward from wholly offscreen rectangles.
  9000: Inward shadows with unequal horizontal and vertical offsets.
 11000: Box-blurred rectangles with borders and inward shadows.
 13000: Unblurred rectangles with fractional placement at screen boundaries.
 15000: Visible borders around rectangles whose fills are wholly offscreen.

run-origin.ass covers text runs crossing the screen edge or a rectangular
clip boundary, including leading spaces and opaque boxes. The visible glyphs
exercise fractional placement when the beginning of the run lies outside
the visible region.
